  "code": "import sys\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    t = int(data[1])\n\n    # The row m+1 sum equals the number of integers x in [0, m] such that\n    # (x xor m) has exactly popcount equal to ... Actually known result:\n    # sum of row m+1 equals 2^{popcount(m)} if m is such that ... Let's derive.\n    #\n    # From the known problem (Codeforces 261C? Actually \"Maxim and Matrix\"),\n    # the sum of the last row for parameter m equals 2^{number of 1-bits in m}\n    # only when m+1 is a power of two? No.\n    #\n    # Known solution: The sum in row m+1 equals t iff m+1 has exactly\n    # k+1 ones in binary where t = 2^k? Let's recall the actual result.\n    #\n    # The matrix is Pascal-like with xor. The value in row m+1, column j\n    # (0-indexed) is C(m, j) mod 2. Sum over j of C(m,j) mod 2 = 2^{popcount(m)}.\n    # So sum = 2^{popcount(m)}.\n    #\n    # We need count of m in [1, n] with 2^{popcount(m)} = t.\n    # So t must be a power of two, t = 2^k, and we need popcount(m) = k,\n    # m in [1, n].\n\n    if t & (t - 1) != 0:\n        print(0)\n        return\n\n    k = t.bit_length() - 1  # need popcount(m) == k\n\n    # Count numbers m in [1, n] with exactly k set bits.\n    # Standard digit DP over binary representation of n.\n\n    bits = bin(n)[2:]\n    L = len(bits)\n\n    from functools import lru_cache\n\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def dp(pos, tight, ones):\n        if ones > k:\n            return 0\n        if pos == L:\n            return 1 if ones == k else 0\n        limit = int(bits[pos]) if tight else 1\n        total = 0\n        for d in range(limit + 1):\n            ntight = tight and (d == limit)\n            total += dp(pos + 1, ntight, ones + d)\n        return total\n\n    total = dp(0, True, 0)\n    # Exclude m = 0 (which has popcount 0). If k == 0, m=0 was counted.\n    if k == 0:\n        total -= 1\n    print(total)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()",
